; aic-run: every test of arm-intc.library on this machine, one after the other; the results are added to aic-results.txt.
; Usage: CD to the folder that holds aic-run, aic-probe, aic-test and arm-intc.library, then: Execute aic-run
; A step that fails stops the run before the next, more daring one. Nothing is installed: the library is opened from this folder.
; Each step closes the results file before the next starts: if the machine stops, what came before is on the disk.

FailAt 21
Stack 20000

Echo "*N*N################ aic-run 0.4" >>aic-results.txt
Date >>aic-results.txt
Version >>aic-results.txt
Version arm-intc.library FILE >>aic-results.txt
Avail >>aic-results.txt

Echo "*N=== 1. aic-probe, read only" >>aic-results.txt
aic-probe >>aic-results.txt
If WARN
    Echo "*N=== stopped: the read only probe failed" >>aic-results.txt
    Skip End
EndIf

Echo "*N=== 2. aic-probe TIMER N=100, a real line without the library" >>aic-results.txt
aic-probe TIMER N=100 >>aic-results.txt
If WARN
    Echo "*N=== stopped: the real line failed without the library" >>aic-results.txt
    Skip End
EndIf

Echo "*N=== 3. aic-test N=100, the library" >>aic-results.txt
aic-test LIB=arm-intc.library N=100 >>aic-results.txt
If WARN
    Echo "*N=== stopped: the library failed a test" >>aic-results.txt
    Skip End
EndIf

Echo "*N=== 4. aic-test STORM, the storm guard" >>aic-results.txt
aic-test LIB=arm-intc.library N=10 STORM >>aic-results.txt
If WARN
    Echo "*N=== the storm test failed" >>aic-results.txt
    Skip End
EndIf

; Last: it reads the pixelvalve of the HDMI output, which may stall the bus if the firmware left it unpowered (no HDMI picture)
Echo "*N=== 5. aic-test VBLANK, the vertical blank of the HDMI output (VideoCore.card on a VC4)" >>aic-results.txt
aic-test LIB=arm-intc.library N=10 VBLANK >>aic-results.txt
If WARN
    Echo "*N=== the vblank test failed" >>aic-results.txt
    Skip End
EndIf

Echo "*N=== all steps passed" >>aic-results.txt

Lab End
Avail >>aic-results.txt
Echo "aic-run: done, the results are in aic-results.txt"
